 proposed, with major or minor contributions in the field of optimal route selection to convey packets in different types of communication networks under various user QoS requirements. This paper provides a comprehensive review of the literature on the topic. The review is structured in a way that shows how network characteristics and requirements were gradually considered over time. Classification criteria are proposed to present and qualitatively compare existing RL-based routing protocols."}]", "excerpt_truncated": true, "source_sha256": "0b703718e0389b969bb7031cddad299f0e4ba7d573d0747e07cb40594a3d1d64", "verification_required": true, "topic_domain": "emergent_preferences", "evidence_role": "discovery", "host_tier": "discovery", "source_identity": null, "persistent_identifiers": ["doi:10.5445/ir/1000118270", "doi:10.1109/access.2019.2913776", "openalex:W2785324569"], "source_candidates": ["https://doi.org/10.5445/ir/1000118270", "https://publikationen.bibliothek.kit.edu/1000118270", "https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/ielx7/6287639/8600701/08701570.pdf", "https://doi.org/10.1109/access.2019.2913776"], "source_candidate_identities": {}}

